The card faces are PNG renderings of Byron Knoll's Vector Playing Cards,
which he released into the public domain in March 2011:

  "I am releasing the images into the public domain. This means that they
  can be used for any purpose without any attribution (although attribution
  would be appreciated)."
    -- https://web.archive.org/web/20110413150009/http://byronknoll.blogspot.com/2011/03/vector-playing-cards.html

  "These images are released into the public domain - attribution is
  appreciated but not required."
    -- https://web.archive.org/web/20110410064033/http://code.google.com/p/vector-playing-cards/

With thanks to Byron Knoll. Knoll notes that his ace of spades is based on
artwork by Suzanne Tyson.

Each file is named for the card's Breakout ticker: D, then the rank
(A 2-9 T J Q K), then the suit (S H D C). DJK is the joker.
